.*
.* WRKJOBD and DSPJOBD: the job descriptions of a library or the list,
.* and what one holds.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=VALCL BASETYPE='CHAR 20'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=JOBD CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=TEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=USER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=SYNTAX CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=HOLD CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=ENDSEV CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=JOBDATE CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=SWS CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=INQMSG CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=JOBPTY CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=JOBQ CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=JOBQLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OUTPTY CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=PRTDEV CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OUTQ CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OUTQLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LOGLVL CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=LOGSEV CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=LOGTXT CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=LOGCLPGM CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=LOGOUT CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=ACGCDE CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=PRTTXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=RTGDTA CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=RQSDTA CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=DEVRCY CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=TSEPOOL CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=MSGQMX CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=MSGQFL CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=ALWMLT CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=ASPGRP CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=SPLFACN CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=DDMCNV CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=INLLIBL CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=PADVAR CLASS=VALCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=JOBDS VARS='OPT JOBD LIB TEXT'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/WRKKEYS' NAME=WRKKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display names only
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:EKEYL.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/DSPKEYS' NAME=DSPKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKJOBD KEYL=WRKKEYS HELP=WRKJOBD ENTER='RETURN 1'.Work with Job Descriptions
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=JOBDS ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJOBD/OPTIONS' OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='CMD ?CRTJOBD JOBD(&LIB./&JOBD.)'.1=Create
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJOBD/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CHGJOBD JOBD(&LIB./&JOBD.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJOBD/OPTIONS' OPTION=3 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CRTDUPOBJ OBJ(&JOBD.) FROMLIB(&LIB.) OBJTYPE(*JOBD)'.3=Copy
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJOBD/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DLTJOBD JOBD(&LIB./&JOBD.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT HELP='WRKJOBD/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPJOBD JOBD(&LIB./&JOBD.)'.5=Display
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKJOBD/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/JOBD' VAR=JOBD USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES.Job Description
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LIB' VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES.Library
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/TEXT' VAR=TEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 2, 3 and 5 or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPJOBD KEYL=DSPKEYS HELP=DSPJOBD ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Display Job Description
:DATA DEPTH=2 COMPACT.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JOBD' VAR=JOBD USAGE=OUTPUT.Job description
:DATAIX VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT.
:DATAIXT.Library
:EDATA.
:DATA DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/USER' VAR=USER USAGE=OUTPUT.User profile
:DATAI HELP='FLD/SYNTAX' VAR=SYNTAX USAGE=OUTPUT.CL syntax check
:DATAI HELP='FLD/HOLD' VAR=HOLD USAGE=OUTPUT.Hold on job queue
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ENDSEV' VAR=ENDSEV USAGE=OUTPUT.End severity
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JOBDATE' VAR=JOBDATE USAGE=OUTPUT.Job date
:DATAI HELP='FLD/SWS' VAR=SWS USAGE=OUTPUT.Job switches
:DATAI HELP='FLD/INQMSG' VAR=INQMSG USAGE=OUTPUT.Inquiry message reply
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JOBPTY' VAR=JOBPTY USAGE=OUTPUT.Job priority (on job queue)
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JOBQ' VAR=JOBQ USAGE=OUTPUT.Job queue
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/JOBQLIB' VAR=JOBQLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/OUTPTY' VAR=OUTPTY USAGE=OUTPUT.Output priority (on output queue)
:DATAI HELP='FLD/PRTDEV' VAR=PRTDEV USAGE=OUTPUT.Printer device
:DATAI HELP='FLD/OUTQ' VAR=OUTQ USAGE=OUTPUT.Output queue
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/OUTQLIB' VAR=OUTQLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAC.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.Message logging
:DATAI HELP='FLD/LOGLVL' VAR=LOGLVL USAGE=OUTPUT.Level
:DATAI HELP='FLD/LOGSEV' VAR=LOGSEV USAGE=OUTPUT.Severity
:DATAI HELP='FLD/LOGTXT' VAR=LOGTXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/LOGCLPGM' VAR=LOGCLPGM USAGE=OUTPUT.Log CL program commands
:DATAI HELP='FLD/LOGOUT' VAR=LOGOUT USAGE=OUTPUT.Job log output
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ACGCDE' VAR=ACGCDE USAGE=OUTPUT.Accounting code
:DATAI HELP='FLD/PRTTXT' VAR=PRTTXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Print text
:DATAC.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/RTGDTA' VAR=RTGDTA USAGE=OUTPUT.Routing data
:DATAC.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/RQSDTA' VAR=RQSDTA USAGE=OUTPUT.Request data
:DATAC.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/DEVRCY' VAR=DEVRCY USAGE=OUTPUT.Device recovery action
:DATAI HELP='FLD/TSEPOOL' VAR=TSEPOOL USAGE=OUTPUT.Time slice end pool
:DATAI HELP='FLD/MSGQMX' VAR=MSGQMX USAGE=OUTPUT.Job message queue maximum size
:DATAI HELP='FLD/MSGQFL' VAR=MSGQFL USAGE=OUTPUT.Job message queue full action
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ALWMLT' VAR=ALWMLT USAGE=OUTPUT.Allow multiple threads
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ASPGRP' VAR=ASPGRP USAGE=OUTPUT.Initial ASP group
:DATAI HELP='FLD/SPLFACN' VAR=SPLFACN USAGE=OUTPUT.Spooled file action
:DATAI HELP='FLD/DDMCNV' VAR=DDMCNV USAGE=OUTPUT.DDM conversation
:DATAI HELP='FLD/TEXT' VAR=TEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:DATAI HELP='FLD/INLLIBL' VAR=INLLIBL USAGE=OUTPUT.Initial library list
.* Not shown: it sets the colon column.
:DATAI VAR=PADVAR USAGE=OUTPUT DISPLAY=NO.Maximum temporary storage in megabytes
:EDATA.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKJOBD.Work with Job Descriptions - Help
:P.The job descriptions of the libraries asked for. Type an option
next to one, or on the first line with a new name to create one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPJOBD.Display Job Description - Help
:P.What a job description gives the jobs that start from it: who they
run as, where they wait and print, how they log and route.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WRKKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F11=Display names only
:PD.Shows the list with the names alone, so more fit on a page.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Repeat position to
:PD.Repeat position to.
:PT.F17=Position to
:PD.Positions the list at the name typed on the command line.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJOBD/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBD'.Job Description
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJOBD/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Create
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to create it. The Create Job
Description (CRTJOBD) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change Job
Description (CHGJOBD) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Copy
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to copy it.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete Job
Description (DLTJOBD) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
Job Description (DSPJOBD) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/DSPKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USER'.User profile
:P.The user profile shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SYNTAX'.CL syntax check
:P.The CL syntax check shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/HOLD'.Hold on job queue
:P.Whether the job or the spooled file is held until someone releases
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ENDSEV'.End severity
:P.The end severity shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBDATE'.Job date
:P.The job date.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SWS'.Job switches
:P.The eight job switches&colon. 0 for off, 1 for on, X for unchanged.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/INQMSG'.Inquiry message reply
:P.How inquiry messages sent to the job are answered&colon. by the
operator, with their default replies, or from the system reply list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBPTY'.Job priority (on job queue)
:P.The job priority (on job queue) shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBQ'.Job queue
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBQLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OUTPTY'.Output priority (on output queue)
:P.The output priority (on output queue) shown for what the display is
about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PRTDEV'.Printer device
:P.The printer device shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OUTQ'.Output queue
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OUTQLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOGLVL'.Level
:P.The level shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOGSEV'.Severity
:P.A message severity from 0 to 99. Higher numbers mean more serious
conditions.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOGTXT'.Text
:P.The text shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOGCLPGM'.Log CL program commands
:P.The log CL program commands shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOGOUT'.Job log output
:P.The job log output shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ACGCDE'.Accounting code
:P.The accounting code the job's resources are charged to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PRTTXT'.Print text
:P.Up to 30 characters printed at the bottom of every page of the job's
printed output.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RTGDTA'.Routing data
:P.The routing data the subsystem compares with its routing entries to
choose the program the job runs.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RQSDTA'.Request data
:P.The request data placed on the job's message queue for the program to
read.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DEVRCY'.Device recovery action
:P.What happens to the job when its display device has an error&colon. a
message is sent, the request is ended, or the job is ended.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TSEPOOL'.Time slice end pool
:P.Whether the job moves to the base pool when its time slice ends.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MSGQMX'.Job message queue maximum size
:P.The job message queue maximum size shown for what the display is
about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MSGQFL'.Job message queue full action
:P.What happens when the job's message queue fills&colon. the job ends,
the queue wraps, or messages are printed and then overwritten.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALWMLT'.Allow multiple threads
:P.The allow multiple threads shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ASPGRP'.Initial ASP group
:P.The initial ASP group shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SPLFACN'.Spooled file action
:P.What happens to the job's spooled files when the job ends&colon. they
are kept with the job or detached from it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DDMCNV'.DDM conversation
:P.Whether conversations to remote systems for DDM are kept or dropped
when nothing is using them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/INLLIBL'.Initial library list
:P.The initial user part of the library list of the job.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
